    C1 = {a0, a1}, C1 below (=1 r2.C2), C2 below (all r0.C1), C2 below (=1 r0.C2),
    T0, T4, T5 defined with qualified cardinalities over r0, r1, r2 and the nominals

  The at-most merging of a nominal recorded a successor as distinct; later the node that had
  created that successor was merged away, so the successor was pruned (not merged into another
  node) and lost its link. The repair of the distinct set replaced the id by the node it was merged
  into, which for a pruned node is the node itself, so the dead id stayed in the set and the scan
